  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\nIssued at 155 PM CST FRI NOV 6 2026\n\nRather benign weather pattern is forecast across central Alabama\nover the next 7 days. Big story in the short term will be\ntemperatures, especially Sunday and Monday mornings. Models\ncontinue to depict medium to high chances for frost conditions\nboth mornings, with a light freeze possible in the colder\nmicroclimates in the north and east central counties. A decision\non a Frost Advisory for early Sunday morning will likely be \nneeded later tonight/overnight.\n\nConditions are forecast to remain rain free through the remainder\nof of the 7 day period. Temperatures will moderate a bit through\nthe early to middle part of the upcoming work week. However, the\nmodels are advertising another sizable upper level trough\ndeveloping over the eastern half of the country by the end of the\nweek. While this trough will help keep the Gulf shut off and\nmoisture levels low, it will also help to push another cold\nsurface high into the lower 48, taking temperatures back down to\nnear (or below) climatological normals.\n\n/61/",
